ed 'DISSOLVE'; Required value missing at [0].action.transition.direction; Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\" — this is part of one union alternative that includes a transition. That alternative likely is action type... it received 'NODE' and rejected it? Hmm no — the union alternatives are tried with the received object; since type 'NODE' matched no literal, all failed. But the presence of a transition spec in the union means SOME action type uses it. The list of literals I see: CONDITIONAL, BACK|CLOSE, URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME (×3 variants), SET_VARIABLE, SET_VARIABLE_MODE, and one with transition. That last one's type literal wasn't shown in the error (error shows issues per alternative; the transition alternative's type literal might be \"NODE\"... but the error says 'NODE' invalid vs 'BACK'|'CLOSE' etc.).\n\n   Hmm confusing. The modern Figma Plugin API reactions: In the new (2024+) typings:\n   ```ts\n   type Action = \n     | { type: \"BACK\" } | { type: \"CLOSE\" } | { type: \"URL\", url: string }\n     | { type: \"NODE\", destinationId?: string, navigation: Navigation, transition?: Transition }\n     | { type: \"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks: [...] }\n     | ...\n   ```\n   The error shows expected literals \"CONDITIONAL\", \"BACK\"|\"CLOSE\", \"URL\", \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\", \"SET_VARIABLE\", \"SET_VARIABLE_MODE\"... it does NOT list \"NODE\". Hmm, but maybe the \"NODE\" alternative IS the one with transition and its literal is checked elsewhere... The error message would print \"Invalid literal value, expected \"NODE\"...\" if NODE were expected — it doesn't. So \"NODE\" is not valid; navigation to a node must use a different action shape in this API version.\n\n   Hmm wait — maybe the new format splits: action type \"NAVIGATE\"? Not listed either. Let me reconsider: maybe it's `figma.widgets`? No.\n\n   Let me think about the current Plugin API docs (2025): `PrototypeReaction`... Actually I recall the newer API introduced `node