 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\" lines belong to one alternative, and the transition alternative didn't echo a type error (meaning \"NODE\" is its literal). \n\n   Also \"navigation\" key was accepted? For the transition alternative, no \"Unrecognized key: navigation/destinationId\" complaint → they're valid for it. \n\n   So correct reaction format:\n   ```js\n   {\n     action: { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: \"…\", navigation: \"NAVIGATE\"|\"OVER\"|...,\n       transition: { type: \"MOVE_IN\"|\"MOVE_OUT\"|\"PUSH\"|\"SLIDE_IN\"|\"SLIDE_OUT\"|\"SMART_ANIMATE\", direction: \"...\", duration: 0.3, easing: {...} } },\n     trigger: { type: \"ON_CLICK\" }\n   }\n   ```\n   Trigger: \"ON_CLICK\" (not \"CLICK\"). Also \"ON_HOVER\",\"ON_PRESS\",\"ON_DRAG\",\"MOUSE_ENTER\",... For simple click: {type:\"ON_CLICK\"}.\n\n   Transition needs `easing` — Easing object: {type:\"EASE_OUT\"}? Easing types: \"LINEAR\"|\"EASE_IN\"|\"EASE_OUT\"|\"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\"|\"EASE_IN_BACK\"|\"EASE_OUT_BACK\"|\"EASE_IN_OUT_BACK\"|\"BOUNCY\"|\"CUSTOM_CUBIC_BEZIER\". I'll use {type:\"EASE_OUT\"}.\n\n   Direction: required for MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT. Values? Probably \"LEFT\"|\"RIGHT\"|\"TOP\"|\"BOTTOM\" or \"UP\"/\"DOWN\". The error didn't reveal. I'll try \"BOTTOM\" for sheet-in; if invalid, error will list allowed values (validation errors usually enumerate). Nice.\n\n   For DISSOLVE-type transitions — not available anymore? SMART_ANIMATE requires matchLayers. Hmm, DISSOLVE missing from the enum per error. Interesting — maybe DISSOLVE is still valid but requires no direction... error says \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'DISSOLVE'\" — so no DISSOLVE, no SMART_ANIMATE in this union branch?? There's also \"Expected null, received object at [0].action.transition\" as another alternative (actions that don't take transition). And earlier \"Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\" for... hmm there are two transition-ish branches. Maybe one branch: {type:\"SMART_ANIMIZE\"...}. Whatever — I'll use MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH with direction+easing. For plain navigations where I don't care, use \"INSTANT\"? Transition optional? For the transition alternative it required transition? The first line \"Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\" suggests when transition present, easing required. If transition omitted entirely, maybe that alternative fails with \"Required value missing at action.transition\"? The other branch said \"Expected null, received object at action.transition\" = alternative with NO transition (transition must be null) — that's for... hmm.\n\n   Simplest: always provide transition {type:\"MOVE_IN\"/\"MOVE_OUT\", direction, duration, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}} for the 4 links:\n   - 01 GetStarted → 02: navigation \"OVER\"? Hmm what navigation values? Not revealed. Common: \"NAVIGATE\",\"SWAP\",\"OVER\",\"CHANGE_TO\",\"SCROLL\". I'll use \"OVER\" for sheet/menu, \"NAVIGATE\" for others. If invalid, error tells me.\n\n2. swapComponent exists ✓.\n3. Avatar_Risa: component 48×72 with no children shown (c:[] at depth 2 — hmm depth 2 means children's children empty; children list empty?? \"c\":[] — it has NO children? A component with no children but 48×72 — that means it's probably a fill-based component (image fill on the component frame itself). Interesting. So avatar = frame with image fill. Resizing distorts aspect; 48:72 portrait. Hmm — maybe the image inside is a person photo 48×72. In transaction chip (circle 36) I'll resize to fit: use w=24,h=36 centered → aspect preserved ✓ (2:3 = 24:36 ✓). Chip circle 36: 24×36 image centered — crops? No, image fits fully (24 wide within 36 circle), shows shoulders/head small. Fine.\n   \n   Wait — actually probe depth: desc(x, d-1) with d=2 → children mapped with d=1 → their children with d=0 → \"c\" omitted at d=0. avatarRisa c:[] means children array empty at depth1... my desc: if(d>0 && n.chi