s the TOP 30px of image? No wait — the node spans y 6..42; chip clips to 0..36; visible region of image = image's top 30px, positioned 6px down. Head at top of photo would sit 6px lower. Slightly off but fine visually inside a small circle? Hmm.\n\nBetter: make the transaction chip component layout accommodate: rather than fighting, I could change the Transaction Row COMPONENT: make the chip 36×36 and mark default Paytm at (6,6) 24×24. For the avatar row, instead of swapping inside instance, hide nested mark (visible=false — allowed?) and overlay avatar on frame. Is `visible` settable on nested instance child? Standard overrides include visibility — yes, API allows setting visible on instance children (docs: \"You can override: visibility, fills, strokes, effects, text...\"). I'll try visible=false; if blocked, fallback to swap+resize(24,36) with the 6px shift.\n\nHmm wait — actually simpler idea: resize the avatar instance to 36×36? Distortion. Or since avatar Risa is 48×72 (2:3), a 24×36 fits the 36-chip fully if y=0 — blocked. Let me try setting mk.y — if error, use overlay. I'll wrap in try/catch and do overlay fallback in same script:\n\n```js\ntry { mk.y = 0; } catch(e) { // overlay fallback\n  const ov = get(\"4:3\").createInstance(); f3.appendChild(ov); ov.resize(24,36); ov.x=16+12+6; ov.y=y+10+0; mk.visible=false; }\n```\nvisible=false inside try too (may fail).\n\nActually — hmm, wait. Let me reconsider whether x/y is truly blocked. The error said \"in set_x: This property cannot be overridden in an instance: relative-transform\". Perhaps this restriction applies only to setting x on the nested INSTANCE node (ic is an InstanceNode), while setting x on non-instance children (text/vector/frame) inside an instance works? E.g., lb (text) reposition might work. And ic (instance) can't be moved. That matches known behavior? In the editor UI, you can move any child within an instance... I'm not sure about API restrictions for nested instances. Whatever — my try/catch plan handles it.\n\nFor tile2/tile3: skip x entirely (46,12 preserved), resize 22,22, recolor white. But wait — after swapComponent, does position persist at (46,12)? It should — swap keeps the node in place with same parent x/y (position is stored on the node itself; swapComponent replaces node but preserves... hmm, the OLD node's x/y is (46,12) — swapComponent swaps the node in-place; the new node typically retains the old node's position/size? \"Attempts to preserve overrides\" — I'll verify by reading x/y after swap and only adjusting if needed (try/catch).\n\nAlso IMPORTANT: partial state exists now. f1 fully built; f3 partially (sb3, av, search, hist, bal, tile1, tile2 with green fill + swapped icon + error mid-way). I must inspect and repair rather than duplicate. Let me fetch workspace metadata to see exact current children of f3.\n\nAlso the stray `const get=(\"1:33\").createInstance()` line in the first failed script didn't run (syntax error). In the second script: `get(\"1:33\").createInstance(); // noop guard` — oops! I wrote that in Call B script: `get(\"1:33\").createInstance(); // noop guard` — YES that line exists in the second script before sb1! It created a stray status bar instance appended to... createInstance attaches to currentPage by default! It would be floating on the current page (probably page 0 or the workspace). Damn. That stray instance: created via createInstance → appended to figma.currentPage (which page? The MCP session's current page — unknown, possibly 0:1 or last used). I need to find and remove it.\n\nLet me inspect: get metadata of 6:2 + check for stray node. I'll write a cleanup+repair script that:\n1. Lists current children of 6:2 and current page nodes.\n2. Removes the stray status bar instance (identify: INSTANCE of 1:33 directly on a page, not inside a frame).\n3. Inspects f3 children to know what exists.\n\nThen a rebuild script that completes f3 and fixes tile2/tile3.\n\nLet me do the inspection first (read-only).",