{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Very important discovery: The workspace page contains ONLY the 7 components — 01_Onboarding and 03_Home are NOT there! The script rolled back entirely on error? But wait — components from Call A exist, and Call B's f1 creation... The output only shows components at y=1000. No frames at y=0. And strays: empty (good — the noop guard `get(\"1:33\").createInstance()` — hmm, that line DID run in the second script... but no stray found. So the whole script rolled back on error. Interesting — the MCP use_figma tool apparently wraps execution in a transaction/undo that rolls back on error. \n\nAlso I notice in Card / Balance: TWO \"Last Updated Balance\" texts (8:65 and 8:66) — a bug from Call A: I created it twice (once in a `{}` block with opacity 0.75 and once standalone earlier — look at my Call A code: I had `mkText(tBal,\"Last Updated Balance\",...)` directly, then another `{ const lb=mkText(...) ... }`. Yes, duplicated! I must delete 8:66 (or 8:65). Fix that in next call.\n\nSo current state: only the 7 components exist (Call A complete), no frames. Good — clean slate for Call B, rewritten with correct instance-override handling:\n\nLearnings:\n1. resize works on nested instance children; x/y does NOT. Position comes from component. So design components so that swapped icons keep correct positions.\n2. swapComponent presumably preserves position (46,12) — I'll verify after building.\n3. Fix duplicate label in Balance Card component (8:66 remove).\n4. For avatar in transaction row: y can't be set. Options: hide nested mark + overlay on frame, or accept shifted crop. Try setting mk.y in try/catch; fallback: visible=false + overlay instance on frame at absolute coords.\n\nWait, actually maybe I should test whether `visible` can be set on nested instance children. If yes, overlay approach is clean. I'll do try/catch: try { mk.y = 0 } catch → try { mk.visible=false; overlay } catch → leave as is (cropped).\n\nHmm — actually, wait. Let me reconsider: is it really true that x/y can't be set on ANY nested instance child, or only on nested INSTANCE nodes? The failed call was `ic.x=46` where ic is nested InstanceNode. For text nodes (lb.x recentering in tile2/3) — unknown. To be safe, avoid repositioning texts inside instances too: for tile label \"Receive\" — \"Send\" label was centered in component via centerW=114 (x=42 for w=30). \"Receive\" at 12 Semi Bold is wider (~52): if I can't recenter → off-center left-aligned at 42? width 52 → center would be x=31. Off by 11px — noticeable. Alternative: set textAlignHorizontal CENTER + fixed width? Changing text width via resize inside instance: resize allowed ✓; then textAlignHorizontal=\"CENTER\" (property override allowed ✓) → centered within its box. So: lb.resize(114, lb.height); lb.x?? — currently x=42; resize keeps x=42 → box 42..156, center at 99 not 57. Ugh, still needs x=0.\n\nTest needed: can I set x on nested TEXT inside instance? Let me include a probe in the next script: create temp instance of Action Tile, try lb.x=0, catch error, remove instance. Then branch logic accordingly. To keep it robust, I'll write the script with a helper `setPos(node, x, y)` that tries x/y, and on failure uses fallback strategies:\n- For labels: resize to full tile width + x=0 + align CENTER (if x fails, then... hmm x=0 also fails → fallback: keep position, accept).\n\nUgh. Cleaner alternative: REDESIGN the components so instances need NO positional overrides:\n- Action Tile: label as full-width centered text from the start: create text with w=114, textAlignHorizontal CENTER, x=0. Then instance label override only changes characters — auto-recenters ✓ no x needed! Similarly icon: keep at fixed position; all icons 24×24 native → but I set 22×22... make it 24×24 at (45,12)? 24 wide centered: x=(114-24)/2=45. All icons 24×24 native, same position → swap needs NO resize/position ✓. \n- Account Tile: marks all 26×26 native! I resized