{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All four frames built (15:2, 15:164, 15:25, 15:221). But ALL reactions failed validation. The error is informative:\n\nThe action schema does NOT accept `{type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation}`. The error enumerates accepted action types:\n- \"CONDITIONAL\" (with conditionalBlocks)\n- \"BACK\" | \"CLOSE\"\n- \"URL\" (with url)\n- \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\"\n- \"SET_VARIABLE\"\n- \"SET_VARIABLE_MODE\"\n\nNo \"NODE\" action?! That's bizarre — the standard Plugin API `Action` type includes `{type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation, transition}`... Wait, but the error says at [0].action.type: Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'. Hmm, this error seems to come from a DIFFERENT validation schema than the standard plugin API — this MCP environment's use_figma validates reactions against a restricted schema that lacks NODE navigation?!\n\nHmm wait — actually, maybe this is the newer Figma API where navigation actions are expressed differently? Let me think. In the current Figma Plugin API docs, `Reaction` = { action: Action, trigger: Trigger }. Action can be:\n- {type: \"NODE\", destinationId, navigation, transition}\n- {type: \"BACK\"}\n- {type: \"URL\", url}\n- {type: \"CLOSE\"}\n- etc.\n\nThe validator here says action.type NODE is invalid — expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' (in one branch), or CONDITIONAL, URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME, SET_VARIABLE, SET_VARIABLE_MODE. So this schema simply doesn't include NODE?!\n\nThat seems like the MCP server's use_figma sandbox uses a modified/limited validation. Hmm. But wait — maybe the actual API changed: newer versions of Figma might have moved NODE navigation to... hmm, no. As of my knowledge, {type:\"NODE\"} is valid.\n\nHmm, wait — maybe the issue is `navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"`. In the current API, `navigation` values are \"NAVIGATE\" | \"SWAP\" | \"OVERLAY\"... Actually I recall: Navigation enum: \"NAVIGATE\" | \"SWAP\" | \"OVERLAY\" | \"CHANGE_TO\"? Historically it was \"NAVIGATE\" | \"SWAP\" | \"OVERLAY\". The error branches shown are just the alternatives Zod tried; the first branch (CONDITIONAL) rejected because of type mismatch, etc. The NODE action isn't in the enum at all per this validator.\n\nHmm, but actually — maybe this environment's figma global is not the real plugin API but a restricted mock? The components/images worked though.\n\nOptions:\n1. Use `figma.on(\"notification\")`... no.\n2. Try action {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"} — already failed.\n3. Maybe the trigger is the problem? No — error clearly about action.\n4. Try setting reactions via the older property `node.reaction`? No such property. There's `node.reactions` only.\n5. Maybe use \"SWAP\"? The enum didn't include NODE at all.\n\nHmm hold on — re-read the error: \"Expected [0].action to be one of the following, but none matched\" then lists branches:\n- CONDITIONAL\n- 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' (one branch: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE' at [0].action.type\") — interesting! So there IS a branch where type can be BACK or CLOSE. This is the simple-action branch: {type: \"BACK\" | \"CLOSE\"}. \n- URL\n- UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME (several variants)\n- SET_VARIABLE\n- SET_VARIABLE_MODE\n\nSo the validator's Action union = CONDITIONAL | BACK | CLOSE | URL | UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME | SET_VARIABLE | SET_VARIABLE_MODE. No NODE. This strongly suggests the Figma API version in this environment has removed plain NODE actions from `reactions`?? \n\nWait wait. Actually — I recall that in 2025, Figma redesigned prototyping: interactions moved to a new model. Hmm, actually there IS a newer API: `figma.pages`... In the \"new\" prototyping model, `Reaction.action` type \"NODE\" still exists I believe.\n\nAlternatively, maybe this MCP environment intercepts and validates against ITS OWN schema which is outdated or limited. Since we can't change the server, work with what's accepted.\n\nHmm — what about CONDITIONAL? \"Required value missing at [0].action.conditionalBlocks\". CONDITIONAL actions contain conditionalBlocks — blocks of {condition?, actions: [...]}? In the new prototyping API (2024+), there's ConditionalBlock: {condition?: Expression, actions: Action[]}. So a CONDITIONAL action with one unconditional block containing... a NODE action? But NODE isn't valid anywhere per this validator.\n\nHmm, so how do we create \"navigate to another frame\" links at all in this environment? Maybe through... `figma.createFlowStartingPoint()`? Flow starting points exist on pages. But interactions...\n\nWait — maybe the environment is a SIMULATOR (not real Figma)? No — screenshots, metadata all work; it's real Figma.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the reactions property validator in the plugin API NOW expects actions like:\n- {type: \"NODE\", destinationId, navigation, transition} — should be valid...\n\nUnless the REAL issue: `transition` key inside action — one branch complained \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following... Required value missing at [0].action.transition\" — that branch seems to REQUIRE transition. And final line: \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'transition' at index 0\" — meaning in the matched branch (probably the last tried?), transition was unrecognized. This is Zod union noise.\n\nHmm, but \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation' at [0].action\" appears in EVERY branch — meaning no branch accepts destinationId/navigation.\n\nCould the correct current shape be different, e.g. navigation nested inside...? Let me recall the actual current typings (fable-cutoff ~early 2025): \n\n```ts\ninterface Reaction { action: Action; trigger: Trigger; }\ntype Action = NodeAction | BackAction | CloseAction | UrlAction | ...\ninterface NodeAction { type: \"NODE\"; destinationId?: string; navigation?: Navigation; transition?: Transition; }\n```\n\nHmm — NodeAction.destinationId optional, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\" | \"SWAP\" | \"OVERLAY\" | \"CHANGE_TO\". That's what I used. And it failed.\n\nOK here's another thought — maybe THIS file is a FigJam/design... it's a design file. Interactions work in design files.\n\nMaybe the sandbox wrapper validates reactions itself and has a BUG (missing NODE in union). If so, no amount of shape tweaking will pass. Workaround options:\n\nA. Use `figma.currentPage.setPrototypeConnections`? Not a real API.\nB. Use the REST API? Not available.\nC. Create interactions via \"PrototypeConnect\"? Not real.\nD. Hmm — what about `node.reactions` on COMPONENT nodes? Same validator.\n\nActually, let me look at the error once more for the CONDITIONAL branch: \"Invalid literal value, expected 'CONDITIONAL' at [0].action.type; Required value missing at [0].action.conditionalBlocks\". So CONDITIONAL = {type:\"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks: [...]}. What's a conditional block? New API: `ConditionalBlock { condition?: Expression | null; actions: Array<Action> }`. If I put a NodeAction inside conditionalBlocks.actions, the same validator would recurse and reject NODE again... unless the validator for inner actions is different (unlikely).\n\nHmm hold on, maybe I should reconsider: maybe this environment IS an older Figma version where the correct action type is... In the OLD days (2019), reactions were: `node.reaction = {trigger: {type:\"CLICK\"}, action: {type:\"NODE\", destinationId}}`. Old singular `reaction` property! And old format transition {type:\"DISSOLVE\"}. My earlier attempt with old format ALSO failed validation with the same error presumably (summary says old format failed and the error revealed the new format requirements — but actually maybe the error was the same union error!). The summary said: \"Reactions validation error (old format {type:\"CLICK\"}, transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\"}): discovered correct schema from the error message — trigger ON_CLICK; transition must be MOVE_IN/... with required direction + easing\". So the error message did mention trigger ON_CLICK and transitions MOVE_IN etc. — so the validator knows ON_CLICK trigger and MOVE_IN transitions. It enumerated those. And it enumerated actions WITHOUT NODE. Interesting — so the validator: Trigger union includes ON_CLICK (+ others); Action union lacks NODE.\n\nSo in THIS environment, navigation via reactions may be impossible via the type:\"NODE\" action... OR the correct key names differ: maybe destination is \"destinationId\" only when navigation is... hmm \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation'\" — both rejected everywhere.\n\nWhat action shapes remain that can navigate? BACK (goes back in prototype history). CLOSE (closes overlay). Neither creates a link to 03_Home from 01.\n\nHmm... unless \"CHANGE_TO\" navigation with component variants... not applicable.\n\nWait — maybe the validator is Zod-generated from the REST-like \"dev resources\" schema... Whatever. Let me probe systematically in ONE call with many try/catch probes to find ANY accepted navigation action:\n1. {type:\"NODE\", destinationId} only\n2. {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"MOVE_IN\", direction:\"BOTTOM\", duration:250, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}} (done, failed)\n3. {type:\"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks:[{actions:[{type:\"NODE\",destinationId}]}]}\n4. Maybe action type \"NAVIGATE\"? {type:\"NAVIGATE\", destinationId}\n5. {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"CHANGE_TO\", transition:{type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\"...}}\n\nAlso probe trigger formats: {type:\"ON_CLICK\"} vs {type:\"CLICK\"}.\n\nIf NODE is truly absent, alternative: use CONDITIONAL wrapper around NODE — if inner validator differs, great.\n\nLet me write a probe call testing shapes against a THROWAWAY node (create temp rect, try shapes, remove). Keep output compact: record first 80 chars of each error.\n\nActually — one more idea: maybe the environment accepts `figma.util`? No.\n\nAlso possible: the use_figma sandbox exposes `figma` from a specific plugin 