{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All shapes rejected. Even CONDITIONAL with inner NODE. No `reaction` property. No `interactions`.\n\nHmm. So `reactions` only accepts: CONDITIONAL | BACK | CLOSE | URL | UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME | SET_VARIABLE | SET_VARIABLE_MODE.\n\nWait — maybe CONDITIONAL's inner actions validator is the same union, so inner NODE also rejected. But maybe the conditional block schema differs: maybe conditionalBlocks items need `condition` key explicitly? The error for cond was the same union error at [0].action — outer level. The outer CONDITIONAL failed because... hmm, actually if the outer shape {type:\"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks:[...]} was structurally right, the error would be about INNER actions. The error was \"Expected [0].action to be one of the following\" — outer union — meaning the CONDITIONAL branch ALSO failed. Possibly because inner action NODE is invalid, propagated up. Or because conditionalBlocks schema differs.\n\nLet me probe deeper into CONDITIONAL: try with empty actions or with a BACK action inside to see if the CONDITIONAL branch itself validates: {type:\"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks:[{actions:[{type:\"CLOSE\"}]}]}. If that validates, then conditional blocks work, and inner NODE is the blocker (inner uses same union).\n\nGiven NODE navigation seems truly absent... how does one create prototype links in this Figma version?! \n\nThink — maybe in this new API version, navigation is done via a DIFFERENT mechanism entirely: e.g., `figma.onLinkClick`? Or via \"PrototypeFlows\"? Or the new \"interactions\" API might be: `node.setInteractionAsync`? Hmm.\n\nOr maybe... the ACTIONS in the new model: there's a \"DESTINATION\"? The union I saw might be truncated? No — Zod listed all branches.\n\nWait, actually, let me re-read one branch: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE' at [0].action.type\" — this branch accepts type BACK or CLOSE with NO other keys. Another: URL. Another: UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME variants. SET_VARIABLE. SET_VARIABLE_MODE. CONDITIONAL.\n\nHmm what about `CHANGE_TO`?? My probe of {type:\"CHANGE_TO\"} failed with the same outer union error (change_to ERR) — but the truncated message doesn't show whether CHANGE_TO was among expected values. The FULL error from the first call enumerated: CONDITIONAL, BACK|CLOSE, URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME×3, SET_VARIABLE, SET_VARIABLE_MODE. No CHANGE_TO, no NODE.\n\nSo this Figma build's reactions schema has NO direct node navigation. Bizarre... UNLESS: in this version, navigation actions moved to a NEW property: e.g. `node.prototypeReactions`? or the new \"Prototyping\" uses `figma.util`... \n\nHmm, let me think about what Figma actually shipped in 2025: At Config 2025, Figma announced \"Figma Sites\" and \"Figma Make\". Also \"new Prototyping\" with variables/conditionals launched 2024 — actions: Navigate (NODE), Change to (NODE+CHANGE_TO), Open link (URL), Back (BACK), Close (CLOSE), Set variable (SET_VARIABLE), Conditional (CONDITIONAL), plus video actions (UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME). The 2024 API DID include NODE. So a schema lacking NODE is anomalous...\n\nUNLESS the schema split: maybe Navigate action now requires `navigation` BEFORE destinationId? Zod doesn't care about order. \n\nHmm, maybe the issue is different: maybe in this version NodeAction requires destinationId to be a valid node ID **that exists in a prototype-eligible state**, and invalid destination → falls to \"none matched\" with misleading \"unrecognized keys\"?? No — \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation'\" is definitive: the object schema for that branch doesn't have those keys.\n\nNew idea: maybe the correct type literal changed to \"DESTINATION\"? or \"LINK\"? or \"SCREEN\"? Try probing more type literals: \"SCREEN\", \"DESTINATION\", \"LINK\", \"OPEN\", \"GO_TO\". Cheap to probe — the union error lists accepted types though, so guessing shouldn't be needed... but the union error might