\"reactions\\\" failed validation:\" — real Figma errors look like \"in set_reactions: ...\" hmm, actually real Figma validation errors ARE formatted like: `in set_reactions: Property \"reactions\" failed validation: ...`. And real Figma errors DO include long \"Expected X to be one of the following\" enumerations. So this looks like REAL Figma validation. If REAL Figma's validator (Oct 2026 build) lacks NODE... then the API changed post-cutoff (plausible for 2026!). In the 2026 API, how are navigate interactions created? Maybe:\n\n`node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, action:{type:\"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks:[{actions:[{action: {type:\"NAVIGATE\"...}}]}]}}]`? \n\nI can't guess blindly forever. Better: enumerate! Probe a battery of candidate type literals quickly and inspect the FULL error for ONE of them (the error enumerates expected values — I got truncated at 90 chars). The full union error IS the spec. I already have the full union from the first call — it listed everything. So no type literal will navigate except via CONDITIONAL blocks' inner schema (which might differ!).\n\nSo focus on CONDITIONAL: what's its full inner schema? Probe {type:\"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks:[]} (empty) — if branch validates, the error moves to inner. Then add {actions:[{type:\"BACK\"}]} etc. Also probe conditionalBlocks with condition key.\n\nAlso — maybe check `figma addon`: `figma.triggerInteract`? no.\n\nANOTHER practical angle: the deliverable requires \"prototype interactions required by the brief\". If the API genuinely can't create NODE navigate links, fallback options:\n1. URL action with figma:// proto link — janky, not acceptable.\n2. Report limitation.\n\nBut before giving up, probe CONDITIONAL deeply, and also probe trigger validity: maybe with action CLOSE + trigger CLICK (old) vs ON_CLICK to learn trigger union.\n\nLet me also check whether there's some OTHER node property for the new prototype system by scanning `Object.keys(figma)` filtered by /proto|interact|flow|link/i — Object.keys on figma global should work (sandbox may allow enumerating existing keys; accessing values might throw — wrap). Also scan Object.getOwnPropertyNames(rect) for reaction-ish props: rect props include \"reactions\", maybe \"flowStartingPoint\"? (frames have flowStartingPoint? actually PageNode has flowStartingPoints). Probe \"flowStartingPoint\" in frame.\n\nProbe plan (single call, all try/catch, truncate errors to 150 chars):\n1. cond_empty: {type:\"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks:[]}\n2. cond_back: {type:\"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks:[{actions:[{type:\"BACK\"}]}]}\n3. cond_cond: with condition:null\n4. cond_node_full: inner {type:\"NODE\",destinationId,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:{...}}\n5. keys of figma matching regex\n6. \"flowStartingPoint\" in tmp\n7. trigger probes: CLICK with CLOSE action; ON_TAP? HOVER?\n\nReturn compact.","signature":"0a7c12403d0649ea858725dd"}],"id":"35566a68-f969-4ea2-8db2-43da9a21b39e","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc0b1614-1a50-4b76-91ee-9a5812ecc44e","uuid":"c7c011c4-f2ee-4d8c-98ec-f82e930175af","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:25:47.466Z","thinking_duration_ms":48278}
