{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Progress! The SHAPES are now VALID — the error changed from schema validation to semantic: \"destination 15:25 was rejected — ... for NAVIGATE actions, destinations must be a different top-level frame on the same page\". \n\nMy probe source: a RECTANGLE inside a temp frame — rectangles are not valid prototype sources, and 15:25 is a top-level frame on the same page... The error says source may not be a valid prototype source (rectangle isn't) — that's likely the main issue. Get the full error to see the rest of the message (truncated at 300). \"for NAVIGATE actions, destinations must be a different top-level frame on the same page\" — 15:25 IS a top-level frame on the same page. So the failing part is probably the SOURCE (rectangle inside frame not a valid prototype source... actually any object in a frame can have interactions in Figma; hmm, but maybe this version requires... whatever).\n\nThe real links: btn1 (an INSTANCE inside f1) → f2; instance as source should be fine. So wire the actual links now:\n\n- btn1 (15:20) → 15:164: {type:\"NODE\", destinationId:\"15:164\", navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"MOVE_IN\", direction:\"BOTTOM\", duration:250, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}, matchLayers:true}}\n- cancel (15:178) → 15:2: MOVE_OUT BOTTOM same easing\n- btn2 (15:188) → 15:25: transition null\n- av (15:37) → 15:221: MOVE_IN LEFT\n- scrim4 (15:245) → 15:25: transition null\n\nNode lookup: get(\"15:20\") etc. — cross-call get() of previously created nodes FAILED last time (13:2 null). Use ws.findOne(n=>n.id===\"15:20\")? findOne on page children recursively — works. Or name-based lookup. Safer: collect via ws.findAll(n=>[\"15:20\",\"15:178\",\"15:188\",\"15:37\",\"15:245\"].includes(n.id)). If empty → frames vanished again?! Check first: count frames.\n\nAlso verify frames still exist (persistence worry). Do it in same call: find the 5 nodes; if all found, set reactions; return summary + reaction verification (JSON.stringify of node.reactions after set).\n\nEach reaction set wrapped in try/catch collecting errors.","signature":"cb16bbce73d44b678775b2e1"}],"id":"59839282-a7c0-4418-9cef-d3fb7ca787da","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc0b1614-1a50-4b76-91ee-9a5812ecc44e","uuid":"d7ffc589-c8cb-45c3-9688-4b5eb3091f57","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:27:38.065Z","thinking_duration_ms":9666}
