lushing?! The TypeError call left the rect in the real file! Confirmed by 8:12 \"Rectangle\" 10×10 at (0,0). Damn — so errors DON'T roll back; everything flushes. The \"rollback\" theory was wrong all along — every call flushed, including partial/failed ones!)\n\nRevised understanding:\n- Every use_figma call flushes ALL changes to the real file, even when the script throws mid-way.\n- The session's document VIEW is stale (cross-call getNodeById for new nodes returns null; ws.children stale).\n\nThat explains everything:\n- 13:x build succeeded + flushed. Next call (02/04 build) get(\"13:2\") → null (stale view). Its script threw → nothing flushed → real file unchanged (13:x remained).\n- Listing call → stale view (no frames).\n- Mega-build 15:x → appended to ws (stale view = components only) → created a SECOND set of frames → flushed. Real file now has BOTH 13:x and 15:x sets (DUPLICATES!).\n- Probes flushed their temp stuff: 8:12 leftover rect (from the TypeError call — created before the throw).\n- Wiring call: stale view → found nothing → no reactions written.\n\nSo now I must:\n1. Delete the DUPLICATE 13:x frames (13:2, 13:25) and stray 8:12.\n2. Write the 5 reactions on the 15:x nodes.\n\nBut the stale-session problem: how do I reference real-file nodes from the session? The session view is stale... Maybe the session REFRESHES on each call but the refresh lagged? The wiring call was right after probe calls. Time has passed now (get_metadata round-trip). Maybe a fresh call now sees the real state? Worth testing: a read-only call listing ws.children. If it shows everything, great — proceed with cleanup+reactions in the same or next call.\n\nActually, be careful: if the session view is stale and I create/delete based on stale info, I make MORE duplicates. Strategy: single call that (a) re-reads ws.children fresh, (b) deletes duplicates by ID if found (13:2, 13:25, 8:12), (c) sets reactions on 15:x nodes if found. If the view is STILL stale (shows only components)