"+e.message.slice(0,200); } };\nconst out={};\nconst m=[[\"15:20\",\"15:164\",T(\"MOVE_IN\",250,\"BOTTOM\")],[\"15:178\",\"15:2\",T(\"MOVE_OUT\",250,\"BOTTOM\")],[\"15:188\",\"15:25\",null],[\"15:37\",\"15:221\",T(\"MOVE_IN\",250,\"LEFT\")],[\"15:245\",\"15:25\",null]];\nfor(const [src,dst,tr] of m){ const n=figma.getNodeById(src); if(n) out[src]=set(n,dst,tr); else out[src]=\"NOT_FOUND\"; }\nres.reactions=out;\nreturn JSON.stringify(res);\n```\n\nHmm — but if the session view is stale, getNodeById(\"13:2\") returns null and remove does nothing (fine), reactions NOT_FOUND (need retry later). But WAIT — danger: if the session view is stale but FLUSHES anyway, does flushing a session whose view lacks frames DELETE the real frames?! The mega-build session view presumably didn't have 13:x... and 13:x SURVIVED the mega-build flush. So flush = incremental changes, not full-state overwrite. Safe.\n\nAlso the 15:x reaction destination IDs: btn1 15:20 → dest 15:164 ✓ etc.\n\nOne more consideration: the duplicate 13:x frames are EXACT duplicates of 15:x? Compare metadata: 13:2 vs 15:2 — identical structure. 13:25 vs 15:25 — identical. Delete 13:2 and 13:25. Also stray 8:12 rect at (0,0) 10×10 (sits at workspace origin, would pollute 01_Onboarding area? It's at (0,0) — INSIDE 01_Onboarding's bounds but it's a sibling on the page, z-below the frames? It was created AFTER components... it's listed BEFORE the frames in metadata order. Frames drawn later → on top. A 10×10 rect at (0,0) on the page: inside 01 frame's area but as a page-level sibling, it renders BEHIND/OVER? Page-level siblings render in canvas order; the frame 01 covers (0,0)-(390,844) — the rect would be underneath 01's opaque BG → invisible. Still, delete it for cleanliness.\n\nAlso — hmm, \"8:12\" — I should double check it's my stray, not something pre-existing. Metadata of the page at the very beginning (from earlier session): the summary said \"workspace contains only the 7 components... NO frames exist yet\"