e creates a solid white blob = square!)\n- Banner icon: blue square (same — recolored to blue, solid blob)\n- Eye on balance card: white square/circle\n- Logout: red square\n\nSo the root cause is clear: **my recolor() helper recolors every solid fill to the same color, and these line icons are built from multiple filled shapes where recoloring all to one solid color + they overlap → solid blob**. But wait — menu icons recolored? No — menu icons stayed #1A1A1F (default), and they render fine. The Logout icon is the only recolored one in the menu, and it's broken. In Home: search (gray), history (white), send/receive/scan (white), offer (blue), eye (white) — all broken. Everything NOT recolored renders fine.\n\nWait, but why would recoloring turn a glyph into a SQUARE? Unless the icon components contain a bounding-box rect... Hmm. OR — the recolor helper also recolored *strokes*... that wouldn't make a square either.\n\nAlternative hypothesis: the recolored nodes aren't the icon instances at all — maybe my helper recolored the chip/container BEHIND the icon, and the icon instance inside failed to swap, remaining... no.\n\nHmm wait, actually let me reconsider. In the Send tile: white rounded SQUARE ~28×28 at top-left area. If the icon instance is 24×24 white and the glyph is made of e.g. a filled triangle+shapes with all-white fills, the union could look square-ish? A send (paper plane) glyph filled solid white would look like a triangle, not a square. The screenshot shows clean rounded squares — more like chip backgrounds.\n\nLet me actually inspect the structure of 15:83 (Tile/Action instance) and its icon sublayers, plus 15:39 (Icon_Search instance) — check what children/fills exist. Since async fetch works now, I can read real state. Let me also check what the icon instance's main component looks like — e.g., Icon_Send 4:23 structure.\n\nActually, more efficient: screenshot the component 8:14 (Tile/Action) and 8:30 (Banner/Reward), and inspect 15:39/15:44/15:83/15:98/15:247... hmm wait 15:247 is avatar. The logout icon is inside 15:285 (Item/Menu instance at y=760).\n\nPlan: one use_figma read call that dumps structure of:\n- 8:14 (Tile/Action component) — children with fills\n- 15:39 (search icon instance)\n- 15:44 (history icon instance)\n- 15:83 (send tile) — icon child\n- 15:98 (banner) — icon child\n- 15:285 (logout item) — icon child\n- 15:47 (Card/Balance) — eye chip child\n\nDump each node: id, name, type, fills (colors), size, children summary. Then decide fixes.\n\nAlso 04_Menu right side shows the home content dimmed behind — scrim looks fine. Also notice: in 04_Menu the top-right shows the history button as plain black square (icon invisible) and balance card eye as white square — consistent with Home issues.\n\nLet me run the structural dump.","signature":"5e3b548a189f45da9d6e842f"}],"id":"141ef901-652f-4ac6-9fb9-f10335ee28e8","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc0b1614-1a50-4b76-91ee-9a5812ecc44e","uuid":"70a6028a-28d6-495d-b118-b3e7a2410ffe","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:07:36.663Z","thinking_duration_ms":26181}
