d to my view, the white ring (12px margin each side) might have been hard to see against the light BG — the white circle blends with the near-white background #F5F6FA! YES — that's it. The white circle was there all along, invisible against near-white BG; the black square dominated. Now with icon cleared: white circle on near-white BG = looks like plain white circle. Consistent!\n\nSo the design has always had a white history button — probably MY earlier build set it white intentionally? Hmm, was it? A white circle with dark glyph on light BG needs a border/shadow to be visible. My Search pill is white with border. For consistency: history button = white circle with BORDER (like search pill) + ink glyph? OR black circle + white glyph (stronger contrast, matches screenshot 1's read).\n\nThe first screenshot read as a BLACK button — strong anchor point in the header. But that was the broken icon. True design intent from my earlier build session: I named it \"History button\" with Icon_History inside; I likely styled it as a white circle with border + ink icon (mirroring the search pill). I can't recall exactly.\n\nDecision: make history button a white circle with BORDER #E7E8EE (1px) and INK glyph — consistent with search pill styling, subtle iOS look. Wait — but the vectors are currently WHITE (my recolor). I'd need to recolor vectors back to INK. Alternatively black circle + white glyph: only need fills=[INK], vectors stay white. Less changes, strong contrast, matches first screenshot appearance. GO WITH BLACK CIRCLE + WHITE GLYPH.\n\nFix call:\n```js\nconst ink = solid(\"#1A1A1F\");\n15:43.fills=[ink]; 15:227.fills=[ink];\nconst t88 = (await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"15:88\")).children.find(c=>c.type===\"INSTANCE\"); t88.fills=[];\nsame for 15:93, 15:285;\n```\nThen verify vector colors of nested receive/scan/logout icons (dump strokes) — if not white/red as expected, fix them too in same call:\n- receive vectors: ensure WHITE\n- scan vectors: ensure WHITE  \n- logo